  "id": "relative-refractory-period",
  "term": "relative refractory period",
  "definition": "The relative refractory period is the phase after an action potential when a cell is recovering its excitability. During this time, the cell can respond again, but only to a stronger-than-usual stimulus, and that extra strength needed gradually returns to normal.",
